module sync_reset_ff (clk, rst, d, q, qbar);
input clk, rst, d;
output q, qbar;
reg q, qbar;
always @(posedge clk) begin
if (rst) begin
q <= 1'b0;
qbar <= 1'b1;
end
else begin
q <= d;
qbar <= ~d;
end
end
endmodule

A tri-state buffer can be implemented in Verilog using a module with an output that is tri-stated (high-Z) when the enable signal is low. The output can be driven by either the input signal or a high-Z state depending on the enable signal. Here is an example implementation:

`timescale 1ns/10ps

module tri_state_buffer (input logic en, input logic din, output logic dout);

assign dout = (en)? din : 1'bz;

endmodule
